                <pb facs="0232" n="172" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg172"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr.
                            Denby</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-11-21"><hi rendition="#italic">November 21,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1205.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your No. 2390, of the 7th ultimo, incloses
                    copy of the imperial edict degrading the ex-viceroy, Liu Ping-chang, for his
                    connection with the Szechuan riots.</p>
                <p>The Department has read this edict with gratification. It is believed that the
                    punishment of the ex-viceroy will be a salutary example, and that the punishment
                    of all implicated subordinate officials is practically pledged thereby.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
